# Story page: nm-challenge
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = Nightmare: Avalanche
---
The Quarry woke in a temper, and rocks fell as though the sky were nursing a grudge it had kept for centuries.

The old tortoise watched from a safe distance. 'I did warn you,' he said to no one in particular, with the deep satisfaction of the person who warned.

{name} dodged, and wove, and bonked. Mostly bonked. It is a difficult thing to be a hero in a rockslide, and nobody hands out medals for trying.
